cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  QDE — a reproducible data-engineering framework for benchmarking quantum and
  classical reservoir computing on chaotic time series
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite the thesis below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Madapuji Srinivasan
    given-names: Badrish
    affiliation: Constructor University
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A leakage-safe, content-addressed and fully traceable benchmark comparing
  gate-based quantum reservoir computing against tuned classical reservoir
  methods (echo state networks, next-generation reservoir computing, and an
  extreme-learning-machine random-feature control) on four chaotic systems. No
  evaluated quantum configuration outperformed the strongest classical
  comparator under a matched measured-feature budget.
keywords:
  - reservoir computing
  - quantum machine learning
  - chaotic time series
  - forecasting
  - reproducibility
  - data engineering
references:
  - type: thesis
    title: >-
      A Reproducible Data-Engineering Framework for Benchmarking Quantum and
      Classical Reservoir Computing on Chaotic Time Series
